WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.495 --> 00:00:12.696
Here we go.

00:00:13.597 --> 00:00:16.199
That's basically it,
and that'll be the reel system

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:18.435
to reel all the line in as that
sled goes up.

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:20.637
All that's left to do
is to string up the cordage.

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:23.040
I gotta couple strands of cord and

00:00:24.074 --> 00:00:26.309
going to replace that other cordage
I was using

00:00:26.309 --> 00:00:29.646
because that stuff was just too stretchy
It wasn't working well.

00:00:31.014 --> 00:00:32.916
Start up at the top.

00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:35.919
So I put it through the block and tackle.

00:00:38.922 --> 00:00:41.458
I think we're going to get it done.

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:44.861
I had my doubts this morning, but

00:00:44.928 --> 00:00:47.064
not so much anymore.

00:00:47.064 --> 00:00:49.700
Oh, yoo hoo! Hey.

00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:50.867
Hi!

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:51.968
Yup?

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.504
Daddy this is so lovely.

00:00:55.072 --> 00:00:56.673
It is so lovely.

00:00:58.508 --> 00:01:00.210
Good night.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.411
Wow, hon.

00:01:01.411 --> 00:01:04.581
You've been working hard.

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:06.349
It is such a good thing

00:01:06.349 --> 00:01:09.286
that this generator shed
is done and built.

00:01:09.853 --> 00:01:10.854
Next!

00:01:10.854 --> 00:01:13.423
And we can get these little generators
back inside.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.659
We don't have to worry.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:17.594
We're more secure with our electricity.

00:01:19.062 --> 00:01:20.263
I think it's cuter than

00:01:20.263 --> 00:01:26.403
I thought it was going to be,
but Caleb doesn't build small things,

00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:29.773
and he doesn't build ugly things, so

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.976
I don't know why I'm surprised.

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:34.945
It's awesome!

00:01:35.378 --> 00:01:37.614
That sheet is on.

00:01:37.614 --> 00:01:40.117
Are you jumping down
or do you need the ladder?

00:01:41.284 --> 00:01:43.186
I'm going to jump.

00:01:43.186 --> 00:01:45.889
Oh Gilbert would be so jealous.

00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:46.957
Nice roof.

00:01:50.794 --> 00:01:52.729
Getting a bite.

00:01:58.235 --> 00:01:59.803
Got some lunch RJ.

00:02:00.337 --> 00:02:00.637
Good!

00:02:01.138 --> 00:02:01.838
Black bomber.

00:02:01.838 --> 00:02:04.341
We can keep this and eat it. Nice.

00:02:04.341 --> 00:02:05.642
That'll be good.

00:02:05.642 --> 00:02:06.409
Oh, yeah.

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:08.411
Yes. You want to open that up for me?

00:02:08.411 --> 00:02:10.447
We'll throw them right in the [INAUDIBLE]

00:02:15.619 --> 00:02:17.254
Yeah, what do you think
about going and trying up

00:02:17.254 --> 00:02:19.623
this rockfish for a snack and
heading home?

00:02:19.623 --> 00:02:22.092
Sure. Sure.

00:02:22.092 --> 00:02:25.796
It was a really beautiful day,
but it's time to go home.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.565
She's going home with some king salmon,

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:31.835
and she's going home with some deer meat
and stuff like that, but

00:02:31.835 --> 00:02:34.971
for her to take fish home that we caught
together today, it would have just meant

00:02:34.971 --> 00:02:36.973
that much more to her,
knowing she was part of it,

00:02:36.973 --> 00:02:39.409
but she's certainly not going to go home
empty-handed.

00:02:40.677 --> 00:02:43.847
I'm going to find us a nice, calm place
out of the wind and cook up some rockfish.

00:02:44.514 --> 00:02:46.283
It sounds good. I'm hungry.

00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:47.417
Let's get out of here. Alright.

00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:49.386
You know, we're out on the ocean.

00:02:49.386 --> 00:02:50.987
We're out on the land.

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:54.424
We're giving it the utmost respect,
and we're trying to

00:02:55.892 --> 00:02:59.129
harvest the animals that we're after
or harvest the fish that we're after.

00:02:59.129 --> 00:03:01.097
If we don't get them

00:03:01.198 --> 00:03:03.266
we're still out here
living our Alaskan dream.

